---
/**
 * How the French sounds: how fast, and in which voice.
 *
 * It sits beside the reading switch because that is where this section keeps
 * the things you set once and forget, and because audio is now on every page
 * that has French on it — a control buried inside one exercise governed the
 * whole section from a place most of it could not see. The voice picker used
 * to live inside *Say it out loud*, which is the only exercise on one pack.
 *
 * Hidden until the page knows there is a French voice to use. A device with
 * none gets no speakers either, so a speed control would be setting the pace
 * of something that never plays. `sayfrench.ts` unhides it, fills it in and
 * wires it up; with no JavaScript it stays hidden, which is correct, because
 * without JavaScript nothing speaks.
 *
 * The voice half is hidden separately, because most phones carry exactly one
 * French voice and a menu with one entry is furniture.
 */
---
<div class="fraudio noprint" id="fraudio" hidden>
  <span class="fraudio-item">
    <label for="fr-speed">Speed</label>
    <select id="fr-speed"></select>
  </span>
  <span class="fraudio-item" id="fr-voicewrap" hidden>
    <label for="fr-voice">Voice</label>
    <select id="fr-voice"></select>
  </span>
</div>

<style>
  /* Scoped styles do not reach what JavaScript creates, but everything here
     is in the markup above — the options are appended to these selects, and
     an <option> takes no styling of its own worth setting. */
  .fraudio {
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.2rem 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0.4rem 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .fraudio-item { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .fraudio select {
    font: inherit; color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.25rem 0.35rem; cursor: pointer;
    max-width: 14rem;
  }
  .fraudio select:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }
</style>
